WEBVTT

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:05.070
Let me out! Let me out of here!

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:08.660
I know you can hear me!
Who do you think I am?

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:14.740
Are you familiar with the feeling of annoyance, Subete?

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.580
In Japanese, it's written with the characters "May" and "fly."

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:20.710
You are like a pesky fly right now.

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:25.010
Dad?

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:31.090
Stop it! What are you doing?

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:33.730
Dad! What is all this?

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:36.630
I just want to bring Maia back!

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:38.260
Shut him up.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:41.190
Drive.

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:44.710
I heard from Mr. Hayashi.

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:48.110
He said Maia is there on your orders.

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:49.410
Is that true?

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:50.880
And what if it is?

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:54.380
Why?! That's not where Maia should be!

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:57.550
You are not the one to decide that.

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.890
The pilot of that red Vector...

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:10.500
He may be the one chosen by Verbalism.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:13.940
There is a need to verify that.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.810
Impossible!

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:21.240
He can't be... The one chosen by Verbalism...

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:24.010
...was supposed to be me!

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:28.850
At one time, man was one with the world of truth.

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:34.260
But the written word brought forth prosperity and suffering.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:43.530
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin,'</i> <i>you're a divine crown</i>

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:49.540
<i>The kanji for "love" and "grief " look very similar</i>

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:54.940
<i>When I realized that, dawn suddenly broke</i>

00:01:54.940 --> 00:02:00.720
<i>The air was filled with so much</i> <i>silence that "blue" "fought"</i>

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:07.060
<i>When suddenly you slid in to the right of me</i>

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:09.960
<i>Rippling with a clatter</i>

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:12.900
<i>and tangled in red thread</i>

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:17.800
<i>and a 39-degree fever of passion</i>

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:23.240
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin,'</i> <i>you're a divine crown</i>

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:29.310
<i>A crown worn on high with pride</i>

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:34.750
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin,'</i> <i>"soothe" my hidden "heart below"</i>

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:40.760
<i>Its form is too much to handle right now</i>

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.690
<i>God's wisdom, the "h" in "her"</i>

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:46.430
<i>With a tearful, feverish gaze</i>

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:49.370
<i>let's stand side by side</i> <i>and look at tomorrow's moon</i>

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:52.200
<i>(Let's stand side by side</i> <i>and look at tomorrow's moon)</i>

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:59.610
<i>The things you can do are so striking</i>

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:08.010
"Light Up! Your Strength"

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:24.430
The current of the flowing river does not cease,

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:27.770
and yet the water is not the same water as before.

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:32.910
The foam that floats on stagnant pools, now vanishing, now forming,

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:36.280
never stays the same for long.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:41.150
So it is, too, with the people and dwellings of the world.

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:44.390
A building will burn down one year, only to be rebuilt the next.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:48.620
Or perhaps a large house will crumble to become a small one.

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:52.560
One person will die in the morning and another will be born in the evening.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:56.300
In this, we are like the foam of the water.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:59.600
I know neither whence the newborn comes,

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:03.630
nor whither go the dead.

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:07.840
Target sighted! Open fire!

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:09.850
Verbalize.

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:16.920
For whose sake do we trouble our minds over these temporary dwellings,

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:21.490
and why do they delight our eyes?

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:23.250
Ruin.

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:25.630
"Ruin"

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:31.100
In competing for impermanence,

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:34.700
dweller and dwelling are no different from the morning glory and the dew.

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:38.370
Perhaps the dew will fall and the blossom linger.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.880
But even though it lingers, it will wither in the morning sun.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:49.290
Perhaps the blossom will wilt and the dew remain.

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:52.820
But even though it remains, it will not wait for evening.

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:51.290
"New Edition <i>Hojoki"</i>

00:04:52.820 --> 00:04:54.820
The <i>Hojoki</i>, is it?

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:56.950
I'm quite fond of it, you know.

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:01.860
You've always hated it, though.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:07.370
This is Delta Squad. The operation is a failure.

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:09.630
I am the last survivor...

00:05:17.510 --> 00:05:22.480
I warned them they were no match for Sougon with the Book of Verbalism.

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:24.920
How many times has this happened now?

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:29.090
The higher-ups never heed our warnings, and rush to rash decisions.

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:33.160
I'm sure the government wants to see a speedy resolution to the issue.

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:37.400
And we're reliant on government backing to support our operations.

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:40.540
It's not pleasant for us people on the ground,

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:43.940
but the higher-ups must be taking the budget into account.

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:47.240
I wonder if they think we're too much of a budget hog.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:49.340
We're doing the best we can on the measly monthly salary.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:53.850
A barrier, huh?

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:57.550
There is one thing Sakurako Soda stole from me

00:05:57.550 --> 00:06:00.120
in addition to the Vectors.

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:02.180
Your heart?

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:11.600
The Logos Monument, excavated together with the Book of Verbalism.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:13.800
For as long as we have that stone monument,

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:18.610
Sougon can't use the power of the book anywhere near our base.

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:20.610
No matter how powerful he is,

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:24.810
he cannot attack us in the real world.

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:27.120
It's like a game of chicken.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:30.590
Neither of us is able to make a move.

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:33.590
I've become an awful adult.

00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:36.660
Relying entirely on children to fight my battles.

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:40.100
Meanwhile, I hide out in a safe place.

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:42.460
You're not the only one, Sakurako.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:45.260
All of us who are involved in this are the same.

00:06:46.270 --> 00:06:49.100
Is that supposed to be any consolation?

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:54.840
I need to do more of what I can do.

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:04.650
Let's go over the unique capabilities of our Vectors once more.

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:04.650
"Setting Up

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:04.650
Please wait juuust a little longer."

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:09.020
Kaibuki's Vector-1 is a multipurpose type with a wide variety of uses.

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:08.620
"Vector-1"

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:13.360
"Vector-2"

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:14.160
Tsukigane's Vector-2 has superior power and specializes in air superiority.

00:07:13.630 --> 00:07:18.430
"Vector-3"

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:18.770
Kikogami's Vector-3 primarily disrupts the enemy and provides rear support.

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:23.640
"Vector-4"

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:21.340
Tsutomu's Vector-4 is a heavy attacker.

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:24.340
It's suited to hit and away tactics.

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:28.380
"Vector-5"

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:29.110
My own Vector-5 is a high speed and mobility type. It's the swiftest unit.

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:34.380
"Vector-6"

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:31.150
Finally, Uminagi's Vector-6.

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:34.380
It's an ambusher type that excels at reconnaissance as well.

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:37.790
Man, 4 is an unlucky number. I want to switch.

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:39.720
Setting aside Vector-2,

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:44.490
why do we use Vector-1, which has no special functions, so often?

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:46.900
Aquarion's stability when in Gattai

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:51.170
is strongest with you and Akira, according to the reports.

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:54.000
"Must be nice..." Is that what you're thinking?

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.570
What?! I-I wasn't thinking that!

00:07:56.570 --> 00:07:58.310
No need to be embarrassed about it!

00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:00.840
Ah, the joys of puberty!

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:03.680
Says the snot-nosed brat.

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:06.350
--Drop the snot-nosed bit!
--Yowch!

00:08:06.350 --> 00:08:09.020
Do those have to be the names for the Vectors?

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:10.520
What? Are you dissatisfied?

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:13.990
What, what, Akira? You have some other idea?

00:08:13.990 --> 00:08:17.150
I'll hear you out, at least. Go on.

00:08:18.990 --> 00:08:20.500
"Savior-go

00:08:18.990 --> 00:08:20.500
Akira Kaibuki"

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:22.600
Rejected.

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:24.400
Yeah, it's not cute enough!

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:29.770
And if Akira changes his, ours would have to change to match.

00:08:29.770 --> 00:08:33.080
Th-Then I'll be Savior-2...

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:34.610
I'm 02!

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:36.680
Can't you both just be unit 2?

00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:39.520
--Then I'll go with Flower
Karan-go Crystal Blood.
--What...

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:43.120
--Nice! We can shorten it to Flakari.
--...do you people think Vectors are?

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:44.590
Going home?

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:45.590
Yeah.

00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:46.590
Later.

00:08:46.590 --> 00:08:47.620
Bye bye!

00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:49.180
See you tomorrow.

00:08:49.390 --> 00:08:55.630
"Please refrain from

00:08:49.390 --> 00:08:55.630
taking pictures of the staff."

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:52.530
Yeah, "Savior-go" isn't happening!

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:56.290
How do you raise a kid to have him turn out like Akira, anyway?

00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:00.440
Though I've been ordered to monitor him,

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:03.870
I only know Akira Kaibuki as he is when he's here.

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:08.140
Oh, right, my mom had a request for you, Hayato.

00:09:08.140 --> 00:09:09.710
--A request?
--Yup!

00:09:09.710 --> 00:09:12.810
I can't face Master Sougon like this.

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:16.590
I'm leaving early!

00:09:16.590 --> 00:09:19.820
Huh?! Wait, Maia! Again?

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:29.590
Akira Kaibuki, I'll uncover everything there is to know about you.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:33.800
What is that creature?

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:35.740
It's clearly out of place in this town--

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:39.810
no, this world's ecosystem.

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:41.670
What <i>is</i> it?

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:54.460
I will exterminate you!

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:57.360
What are you doing?! Hey!

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:59.600
Don't bully Namisuke!

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:01.100
You're a bad person!

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:02.660
What are you doing?

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:05.530
Are you taking this creature's side?

00:10:05.530 --> 00:10:08.000
Let go! Ouch!

00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:10.530
"Kaibuki"

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:21.320
This is...

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:23.490
"Kaibuki"

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:23.890
What's keeping you? Hurry up and come in.

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:25.380
I'll offer you tea, at least.

00:10:26.990 --> 00:10:29.120
"Kaibuki"

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:29.120
How did he know?

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:32.690
It is not ink which must abide in your brush.

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:35.500
You must let your soul permeate it.

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:38.330
--Yes, Master!
--My grandpa's a calligraphy instructor.

00:10:39.970 --> 00:10:43.960
I wouldn't have expected Akira to bring a friend home.

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:49.010
And such a cute girl, at that.

00:10:49.010 --> 00:10:53.040
I didn't bring her here.
She just followed me on her own.

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:59.390
He says that, but inside he's happy, you know.

00:10:59.390 --> 00:11:02.720
If you don't mind, please keep coming to play with him.

00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:05.820
I'll consider it.

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:11.000
Was it a little too bitter, maybe?

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:12.330
You fool.

00:11:12.330 --> 00:11:16.530
How cowardly. To think you'd serve me poison...

00:11:20.510 --> 00:11:23.050
Thank you. Here's this as thanks.

00:11:23.050 --> 00:11:25.340
Oh, no, I couldn't...

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:30.350
I need to talk this over properly with Dad!

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:40.300
It's been a while since I last came here.

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:44.570
There's no question that the source of the M.J.B.K.s is here.

00:11:44.570 --> 00:11:46.030
It doesn't matter what.

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:49.600
I need to find something--anything-- that will make their fight easier.

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:59.380
I used to be the president's secretary. He's so cold.

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:04.890
--Ow...
--Uh, are you okay?

00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:07.160
Sakurako?

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:08.890
Subete?

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:21.770
It's showtime!

00:12:21.770 --> 00:12:25.070
This illusion that I will now perform

00:12:25.070 --> 00:12:29.480
will make this piping hot <i>oden</i> vanish into my stomach in an instant!

00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:31.280
Sigh, he's at it again.

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:34.620
Mr. Tsutomu Domon on the comedy show.

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:38.350
The view count is growing so slowly, it's sad.

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:42.420
Are you still unable to reach Sakurako?

00:12:42.420 --> 00:12:45.830
Yeah, and I've been messaging her for a while now.

00:12:55.640 --> 00:12:58.870
Hold on, Subete, everyone is looking!

00:12:58.870 --> 00:13:00.640
B-But...!

00:13:00.640 --> 00:13:04.450
To think you, who were Dad's secretary,

00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:06.780
had such a reason for stealing the Vectors...

00:13:08.150 --> 00:13:10.290
To grant your sick mother's wish

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:16.020
to see a Vector, just once, before the end...

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:18.890
Sakurako, you care so much for your mother.

00:13:18.890 --> 00:13:21.060
Wh-Why, yes, I do...

00:13:21.060 --> 00:13:24.030
How can he believe a story like that?

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:27.200
So, has your mother recovered?

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:30.470
Oh, yes! She's fit as a fiddle now!

00:13:30.470 --> 00:13:33.740
A Vector's just the thing to cure what ails ya, you know?

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:35.480
I see. That's great.

00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:37.680
But, I'm sorry...

00:13:37.680 --> 00:13:40.250
When I was just about to return the Vectors,

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:44.820
a heinous robber snuck into my house and ran off with them!

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:47.420
My word! That must have been dreadful!

00:13:47.420 --> 00:13:52.590
I really can't tell him I'm using those Vectors to fight now...

00:13:52.590 --> 00:13:56.770
Then Maia is with those thieves right now?

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:59.230
But I can't ask her any more.

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:04.070
It's a secret to those on the outside that I piloted a Vector in battle.

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:12.450
--Sakurako.
--What?

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:13.850
I'm sorry for doubting you.

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:15.180
Oh, it's fine.

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:18.690
I wasn't able to believe in you.

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:22.360
When I heard you had stolen the Vectors,

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:24.760
I thought you had betrayed us.

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:25.730
I'm sorry.

00:14:25.730 --> 00:14:29.300
Um, I'm sorry, too...

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:33.100
To make up for it,
I'll give you anything you want.

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:34.800
No need to hold back.

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:38.040
If I show this, I can get anything.

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:43.110
"From Suginami to the world!

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:43.110
Shinji Hatano's Office"

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:48.450
Oh, this girl.

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:51.420
Don't you think her dance moves are especially sharp?

00:14:51.420 --> 00:14:56.730
And, what's more,
Karan is singing the song solo.

00:14:56.730 --> 00:14:59.830
But that's a commercial that only played locally.

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:02.800
Most people don't even know about it.

00:15:02.800 --> 00:15:07.800
So I'm reaching out to Mr. Hatano, who has the most young followers!

00:15:03.470 --> 00:15:12.340
"Official Candidate of the Reform Party

00:15:03.470 --> 00:15:12.340
From Suginami to the World!!

00:15:03.470 --> 00:15:12.340
Shinji Hatano"

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:13.580
If you would use this commercial,
I'm sure public awareness would go up!

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:15.640
So that Karan can debut as a voice actress,

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:19.780
could I ask you to help spread this girl's voice?

00:15:20.780 --> 00:15:21.920
Ma'am.

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:23.080
Yes?

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:28.360
I'm not familiar with young idols like Karan;

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:32.160
however, I believe grabbing people's hearts

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:34.700
is not so simple.

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:37.200
That goes without saying.

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:40.500
I may not be familiar with idols,

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:43.470
but even if she were able to break out temporarily with the publicity,

00:15:43.470 --> 00:15:47.110
don't the vast majority of them not last long after that?

00:15:47.110 --> 00:15:49.840
It must be the same for voice actresses.

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:52.510
Though I'm not familiar with idols,

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:57.950
I've seen many girls pop up as part of some temporary boom and then vanish.

00:15:57.950 --> 00:16:02.320
I do not wish to see the same happen to Karan.

00:16:01.890 --> 00:16:10.030
"Victory"

00:16:02.320 --> 00:16:05.560
First, she must have a shine brighter than any other.

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:09.830
Is that not more important than trying to become the topic of the day?

00:16:13.170 --> 00:16:14.800
He's hot.

00:16:18.210 --> 00:16:20.210
It's still bitter.

00:16:20.210 --> 00:16:23.010
He said to give you these to help with the aftertaste.

00:16:26.720 --> 00:16:31.210
He's a nice boy. He doesn't like to show it, though.

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:36.090
Has he... always been like that?

00:16:36.090 --> 00:16:38.660
Um, with the savior thing.

00:16:38.660 --> 00:16:41.830
Yes, he's been like that all along.

00:16:41.830 --> 00:16:48.070
Even we aren't sure why he's so hung up on the idea of being a savior.

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:50.610
But, still, this I can say.

00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:55.440
"Savior

00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:55.440
Akira Kaibuki"

00:16:51.670 --> 00:16:55.600
That boy never has the slightest shred of hesitation.

00:16:57.250 --> 00:17:01.850
It's as if he knows what he ought to do from the very beginning.

00:17:01.850 --> 00:17:04.690
What he ought to do?

00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:06.350
What should I...

00:17:06.350 --> 00:17:08.880
Hey, come on! What's wrong?

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:15.460
Okay, now! Tornado Strike!

00:17:16.560 --> 00:17:18.070
See that?

00:17:17.630 --> 00:17:20.530
"Shoko: Where are you now?"

00:17:18.530 --> 00:17:20.530
"Sakurako: Don't worry."

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:27.080
Is it okay for you to do that?

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:28.580
Do what?

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:35.720
"Persia's Behistun Inscription

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:35.720
in Japan for the first time.

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:35.720
On display in the 8F Event Hall."

00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:30.910
To horse around with the common folk.

00:17:30.910 --> 00:17:32.750
I don't mind doing it at all!

00:17:32.750 --> 00:17:36.550
Anyone would be happy to get to be with me!

00:17:36.550 --> 00:17:39.620
Curse your inborn sense of superiority.

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:41.460
--Bye bye!
--Thank you.

00:17:41.460 --> 00:17:43.790
Come back again!

00:17:46.900 --> 00:17:49.390
You never change, do you, Subete?

00:17:51.900 --> 00:17:55.100
I was a little worried about you.

00:17:56.140 --> 00:17:59.910
Your luncheon with
President Ringosberg is at 2:00 PM.

00:17:59.910 --> 00:18:02.280
Following that, you have a business meeting at 3:00.

00:18:02.280 --> 00:18:03.580
Dad!

00:18:03.580 --> 00:18:06.580
Look! I came in first!

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:08.750
Throw the intruder out.

00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:09.580
What?

00:18:09.580 --> 00:18:11.320
This is a place of business.

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:14.320
It is no place for a child to be.

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:15.990
Dad!

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:17.960
Hey, Dad!

00:18:20.130 --> 00:18:23.800
Yeah, there've been times when I was sad.

00:18:23.800 --> 00:18:26.670
But I wasn't alone.

00:18:28.770 --> 00:18:31.540
I had someone to lean on.

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:34.540
That's why I chose to believe.

00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:38.550
Because belief is strength, right?

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:43.820
No matter how cold he is,
Dad will choose me in the end.

00:18:43.820 --> 00:18:47.320
Because I'm the chosen one.

00:18:47.320 --> 00:18:49.390
So, in short,

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:53.020
you'll do nothing yourself and rely on others for everything?

00:18:54.300 --> 00:18:55.790
How unpleasant.

00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:01.060
What?

00:19:10.650 --> 00:19:12.880
Well? Are you getting this?

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:13.880
Huh?

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:17.820
The net is d-down.

00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:22.890
This is the young senator everyone's talking about, Mr. Hatano.

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:26.160
The narration for a platform promotion video.

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:28.600
This is respectable voice acting work too, isn't it?

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:32.600
Well, it's plain, but it's not bad.

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:34.690
Huh? Why?

00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:40.340
Remain calm!

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:44.900
All elevators are currently out of service.

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:48.420
Vector units 1 and 2, system link complete.

00:19:48.420 --> 00:19:51.520
Adjustments to magnetic lane in duct barrel complete.

00:19:51.520 --> 00:19:53.090
All checks green.

00:19:53.090 --> 00:19:54.860
No malfunctions detected in warp gate generation.

00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:56.960
It seems the commander can't make it back right away.

00:19:56.960 --> 00:20:00.430
I will be standing in for her, but don't count on me.

00:20:00.430 --> 00:20:03.460
She comes right out and says things that make it hard to rely on her.

00:20:03.460 --> 00:20:04.570
We're going.

00:20:04.570 --> 00:20:06.130
Verbalize.

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:15.480
"Akira and Maia have launched.

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:15.480
M.J.B.K.'s identity is still unknown.

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:15.480
Hurry back quickly."

00:20:10.770 --> 00:20:15.480
I meant to help, but I'm still completely reliant on the kids.

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:18.750
Sakurako! I'm going to where my father is!

00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:19.750
Huh?

00:20:19.750 --> 00:20:24.590
With all this chaos, I know exactly where Dad will be.

00:20:24.590 --> 00:20:27.960
So I'm going to go there and ask him.

00:20:27.960 --> 00:20:31.390
I'll ask him to give my most important person back to me.

00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:41.970
Time to Gattai.

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:44.570
Sousei Gattai.

00:20:44.570 --> 00:20:46.060
Shout!

00:20:47.340 --> 00:20:48.940
Ah! What?

00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:52.750
Ah, the v-video feed...

00:20:52.750 --> 00:20:54.480
A comms breakdown?

00:20:54.480 --> 00:20:57.620
Dad's just misunderstanding a little.

00:20:57.620 --> 00:20:59.820
So, if I explain it to him properly...

00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:02.320
How sickeningly naive.

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:06.330
Begging your father to give you back the person most important to you?

00:21:06.330 --> 00:21:07.860
What? That's so lame!

00:21:07.860 --> 00:21:09.530
Sakurako?

00:21:09.530 --> 00:21:13.300
She's <i>important</i> to you, isn't she?
Then take her back on your own!

00:21:13.300 --> 00:21:14.840
Don't rely on others.

00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:17.010
"Belief is strength"?

00:21:17.010 --> 00:21:21.140
You're just running away from becoming strong yourself!

00:21:21.140 --> 00:21:22.670
How pathetic!

00:21:24.110 --> 00:21:26.850
Honestly, it's just pathetic...

00:21:26.850 --> 00:21:31.650
Ultimately, I can't do anything, and I'm relying on children.

00:21:31.650 --> 00:21:34.290
I'm horrible.

00:21:34.290 --> 00:21:38.230
I'm sure you can be strong.

00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:41.200
Thank you, Sakurako.

00:21:41.200 --> 00:21:42.730
You're right.

00:21:42.730 --> 00:21:48.040
I need to do more than just believe.
I need the strength to fight.

00:21:48.040 --> 00:21:49.170
I understand now!

00:21:49.170 --> 00:21:51.840
I'll do it! I'll take back Maia!

00:21:51.840 --> 00:21:54.880
Wait, Maia?

00:21:54.880 --> 00:21:56.840
Why can't we Gattai?!

00:21:56.840 --> 00:22:00.750
M.J.B.K., show me your meaning.

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:04.050
Dan! Dan! Dan!

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:06.320
Da-Dan!

00:22:05.590 --> 00:22:07.760
"Sever"

00:22:06.320 --> 00:22:07.760
I will cut it off!

00:22:07.760 --> 00:22:09.890
I will sever my naiveté from myself!

00:22:09.890 --> 00:22:14.400
And take Maia back into my arms!

00:22:14.400 --> 00:22:15.920
Whoops.

00:22:36.420 --> 00:22:39.890
<i>Je-Je t'aime communication</i>

00:22:39.890 --> 00:22:49.890
<i>Oh, you aren't making a bit of</i> <i>eye contact with me while you talk</i>

00:22:49.930 --> 00:22:59.140
<i>Are you texting some far-off</i> <i>neighboring world or something?</i>

00:22:59.140 --> 00:23:04.270
<i>Because this isn't communication at all</i>

00:23:06.210 --> 00:23:12.750
<i>You'd at least understand that much</i>

00:23:12.750 --> 00:23:18.760
<i>even if the times suddenly changed, right?</i>

00:23:18.760 --> 00:23:22.760
<i>Give me je t'aime communication sometimes</i>

00:23:22.760 --> 00:23:26.170
<i>Look at me, answer me, and tell me</i>

00:23:26.170 --> 00:23:32.670
<i>I mean, this is practically</i> <i>like talking to a computer</i>

00:23:32.670 --> 00:23:35.680
<i>A-Adieu application</i>

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:42.320
<i>Even if it means staying lonely</i> <i>in my heart, if it'll connect us</i>

00:23:42.320 --> 00:23:48.690
<i>then, please, at least show</i> <i>your smile to me alone</i>

00:23:50.660 --> 00:23:53.960
Hey, Maia, my Nesta timeline right now is totally wicked!

00:23:53.960 --> 00:23:55.130
Is it that bad?

00:23:55.130 --> 00:23:57.270
"Wicked" is usually a negative word,

00:23:57.270 --> 00:24:00.700
but many modern youngsters use it now with a positive connotation.

00:24:00.700 --> 00:24:03.640
--Say what?!
--That kitty is wicked cute!

00:24:03.640 --> 00:24:04.670
Our language is decaying!

00:24:04.670 --> 00:24:05.770
Maybe it's evolving.

00:24:05.770 --> 00:24:06.770
Next time: Episode 7.

00:24:06.210 --> 00:24:08.210
"Episode 7: Burn It! The Savior's Flames"

00:24:06.770 --> 00:24:08.210
"Burn It! The Savior's Flames."

00:24:08.210 --> 00:24:09.700
Totally wicked! I can't wait!
